<title>UK: UK bus operator bids for Granada unit - paper.</title>
<headline>UK bus operator bids for Granada unit - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's National Express, a privatised bus operator, is one of six shortlisted bidders for Granada Plc's motorway services business Welcome Break, the Times reported on Monday.</p>
<p>The newspaper said Welcome Break, which Granada must sell by April as part of a deal with Britain's Office of Fair Trading, was being sold for an expected 380 million pounds ($638.6 million).</p>
<p>Granada chief executive Gerry Robinson hoped to announce the sale along with other disposals at the company's annual meeting on January 29, said the newspaper.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 6784 ($1=.5950 Pound)</p>
